# Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io), seeded by
# swarm-routing/.github org-sync (`citation = true`; `citation_type` and
# `[[references]]` in .github/org-sync.toml); the repository's own once
# written. Commitizen keeps `version:` in step (`.cz.toml` version_files
# "CITATION.cff:^version:"); swarm-routing/.github tools/zenodo reads the
# concept DOI from `doi:` once the first release is archived on Zenodo.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "BeeAdHoc"
abstract: >-
  BeeAdHoc, the honeybee-inspired routing protocol of Wedde & Farooq (2005),
  as a standalone swarm routing protocol for MANETs: scouts, foragers and an
  energy metric, as a simulator-agnostic C++ core and an ns-3 contrib module
  on swarm-core.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Joppi
    given-names: Daniel Henrique
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6436-8174"
version: "0.1.0"
# The work as a whole; core/ tools/ also MIT OR GPL-2.0-only (LICENSING.md).
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/swarm-routing/BeeAdHoc"
url: "https://github.com/swarm-routing/BeeAdHoc"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24124821"
identifiers:
